IMPORT prelude

-- Row il-53. NOUNS of a paragraph that applies a debt figure, of a figure fixed by a provision, and of an amending instruction and its target. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Insolvency and Economic Rehabilitation Law, 5778-2018, and not of the Execution Law, 5727-1967. It records four things:
-- two printed figures in the Execution Law as an instruction of the Insolvency Law wrote them, the paragraph pair of section 7א2 and the fixed figure of section 76(ג);
-- the Insolvency Law's own wage figures in section 234(א)(1)(א), as enacted; and, as controls, two other instructions of the same chapter with their targets.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the words, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module: `src:` lines are the deposited excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation of the Execution Law
-- (the number after `src:` is the line of the EXCERPT, not of the whole page; the excerpt's own `page line` markers give the page line), and `ext:[SH 2708 ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument.

§ `Nouns of a paragraph with a debt figure`

-- Three kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest. `not read` says that no source was opened for that limb.
-- The consolidation is the only source for what the Execution Law says TODAY: that no later instrument touched the words was not read from any official instrument.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the consolidation only`
    `not read`

-- How the words of a paragraph meet the figure they print. Only the two sides that section 7א2 uses are named.
DECLARE `How a paragraph meets its figure` IS ONE OF
    `it applies when the total debt is at most the figure`
    `it applies when the total debt is at least the figure`

DECLARE `A paragraph with a debt figure` HAS
    `the paragraph is` IS A STRING
    `the figure in shekels` IS A NUMBER
    `the paragraph meets the figure so that` IS A `How a paragraph meets its figure`
    `the consolidation prints the paragraph's figure` IS A NUMBER
    `limb (a): the words as the amending instruction wrote them were read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b): that the present words are those words was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

DECLARE `A section of two paragraphs` HAS
    `the section is` IS A STRING
    `the first paragraph` IS A `A paragraph with a debt figure`
    `the second paragraph` IS A `A paragraph with a debt figure`

§ `Nouns of a figure fixed by a provision`

DECLARE `A figure fixed by a provision` HAS
    `the provision is` IS A STRING
    `what the figure limits` IS A STRING
    `the provision's figure in shekels` IS A NUMBER
    `the consolidation prints the provision's figure` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the words that fix the figure also say it is updated each year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a): the words as the instrument wrote them were read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b): that the present words of the provision are those words was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of an amending instruction and its target`

DECLARE `An amending instruction and its target` HAS
    `the instruction is` IS A STRING
    `the words the instruction brings in` IS A STRING
    `the words found in the target as consolidated` IS A STRING
    `the instruction was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `the target's words were read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
